# Design Systems & UI Standard

Aim for **Apple-quality polish**: precise, restrained, consistent, and considered. Consistency
and craft beat novelty. Every screen should feel like it belongs to the same product.

## Tokens (the single source of truth)

- **Spacing** on a scale (4/8px rhythm) — never arbitrary pixel values.
- **Typography** scale with defined sizes, weights, line-heights, and tracking. Establish a clear
  hierarchy (display → heading → body → caption). Limit typefaces (one or two).
- **Color** as semantic tokens (`bg`, `fg`, `muted`, `primary`, `destructive`, `border`) mapped
  to raw values, themeable for light/dark. Meet contrast requirements at the token level.
- **Radii, shadows/elevation, motion durations, and z-index** are all tokenized.

## Components

- Build on accessible primitives (shadcn/ui, Radix). Theme via tokens; don't fork the primitive.
- Every component supports its full state matrix: default, hover, focus-visible, active, disabled,
  loading, error, empty, selected. Design them all — not just the happy default.
- Variants over booleans (`variant="primary" size="sm"`), typed and documented.
- Document components (Storybook) with every state and usage guidance.

## Layout & composition

- Grid and consistent spacing; align to the rhythm. Generous, intentional whitespace.
- Responsive and fluid from 320px up; content-first breakpoints, not device-specific hacks.
- Optical alignment and balance over pixel-literalism where they differ.

## Motion

- Purposeful: communicates state, guides attention, provides continuity. Never decoration for its
  own sake.
- Fast (150–300ms), natural easing (ease-out for entrances, spring for playful), interruptible.
- Animate `transform`/`opacity` for 60fps. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` — provide a calm
  fallback, never remove essential feedback.

## Content & microcopy

- Clear, concise, human. Consistent voice. Helpful empty and error states with a next action.
- Labels over placeholders for form fields. Never rely on placeholder as the only label.

## Quality bar

- Pixel-consistent spacing and alignment; consistent iconography and weight; no orphaned styles.
- Accessible: contrast, focus, keyboard, labels.
- Feels fast: instant feedback (<100ms), skeletons over spinners, no layout shift.
